  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0174 database is a healthcare-related database that contains information about patients, physicians, nurses, medical procedures, and more. It has 15 tables, each with its own unique purpose and structure.\nThe physician table contains information about the healthcare professionals who work in the hospital, including their names, positions, and social security numbers. The department table lists the different departments within the hospital, along with their names and department heads. The affiliated_with table shows which physicians are affiliated with which departments, along with their primary affiliation status.\nThe medical_procedure table contains information about the different medical procedures that can be performed at the hospital, including their names, costs, and codes. The trained_in table shows which physicians are trained to perform which medical procedures, along with their certification dates and expiration dates.\nThe patient table contains information about the patients who receive care at the hospital, including their names, addresses, phone numbers, insurance IDs, and social security numbers. The nurse table lists the nurses who work at the hospital, along with their names, positions, and registration status.\nThe appointments table contains information about the appointments that patients have with physicians, including the patient's name, the physician's name, the start and end times, and the examination room. The medication table lists the different medications that can be prescribed to patients, along with their names, brands, and descriptions.\nThe prescribes table shows which physicians have prescribed which medications to which patients, along with the date, appointment, dose, and assisting nurse. The block table contains information about the different blocks within the hospital, along with their floor IDs and block codes. The room table lists the different rooms within the hospital, along with their room numbers, room types, floor IDs, block codes, and availability status.\nThe on_call table shows which nurses are on call for which blocks and floors, along with their start and end times. The stay table contains information about the patients who are currently staying in the hospital, including their names, room numbers, start and end times, and physician IDs. The undergoes table shows which patients have undergone which medical procedures, along with the date, physician, assisting nurse, and stay ID.\nOverall, the schemabench_0174 database is a comprehensive and detailed record of the healthcare services provided by the hospital, including information about patients, physicians, nurses, medical procedures, and more. It is organized into 15 tables, each with its own unique purpose and structure, and is designed to provide a clear and accurate picture of the hospital's operations.",
  "gold_question": "Healthcare Management System\n\n1) Background / Context:  \n   The project involves the development of a healthcare management system designed to streamline patient care and administrative processes in a healthcare facility. This system utilizes a relational database to manage comprehensive data about physicians, departments, medical procedures, patients, nurses, appointments, medications, rooms, and facility blocks.\n\n2) Objectives:  \n   - To enhance the efficiency of administrative tasks such as scheduling appointments, room assignments, and medication management.\n   - To improve patient care by providing quick access to accurate patient data and personalized treatment plans.\n   - To ensure regulatory compliance through accurate record-keeping and documentation.\n   - To optimize resource allocation and operational efficiency through automation and data-driven decisions.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users:  \n   - Healthcare Administrators: Manage facility operations, crucial in oversight and compliance.\n   - Physicians & Nurses: Primary users for patient interaction, treatment documentation, and procedure management.\n   - Patients: Service beneficiaries who interact with the system for appointments and feedback.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions:  \n   - Physician Management: Store and manage physician details including employee ID, name, position, and SSN.\n   - Department Management: Oversee departments with information such as department ID, name, head, and affiliations with physicians.\n   - Medical Procedure Tracking: Maintain a database of medical procedure codes, names, and costs.\n   - Patient Management: Handle patient details including SSN, contact information, insurance, and selected primary care physician.\n   - Nurse Management: Record nurse information with details on registration and department assignments.\n   - Appointment Scheduling: Store and manage appointment data, including related patients, nurses, and physicians, with time and location specifics.\n   - Medication Management: Catalog medications by code, name, brand, and description.\n   - Room and Block Management: Manage room allocations and block details for patient stays and resource planning.\n   - History Tracking: Maintain records of patient procedures, stays, and prescribed medications.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions:  \n   - Scalability: Support a growing database of patient and staff information.\n   - Security: Ensure data protection and privacy standards are strictly upheld, particularly for sensitive patient information.\n   - Usability: Provide an intuitive interface for healthcare professionals for quick data retrieval and entry.\n   - Reliability: Ensure system uptime for 24/7 healthcare operations and accurate data management.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_codellama13b/0174.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0174\nCREATE TABLE `physician` (\n  `physician_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `social_security_number` char(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`physician_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `department` (\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `department_head` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`department_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `affiliated_with` (\n  `affiliation_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `physician_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `primary_affiliation` tinyint(1) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`affiliation_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `affiliated_with_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`physician_id`) REFERENCES `physician` (`physician_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `affiliated_with_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`department_id`) REFERENCES `department` (`department_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `medical_procedure` (\n  `procedure_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `cost` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`procedure_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `trained_in` (\n  `training_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `physician_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `procedure_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `certification_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `expiration_date` date NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`training_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `trained_in_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`physician_id`) REFERENCES `physician` (`physician_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `trained_in_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`procedure_id`) REFERENCES `medical_procedure` (`procedure_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `patient` (\n  `patient_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) NOT NULL,\n  `insurance_id` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `social_security_number` char(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`patient_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `nurse` (\n  `nurse_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `registration_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`nurse_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `appointments` (\n  `appointment_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `patient_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `physician_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `examination_room` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`appointment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `appointments_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`patient_id`) REFERENCES `patient` (`patient_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `appointments_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`physician_id`) REFERENCES `physician` (`physician_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `medication` (\n  `medication_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `brand` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`medication_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `prescribes` (\n  `prescription_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `physician_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `patient_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `medication_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `date` date NOT NULL,\n  `appointment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `dose` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `nurse_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`prescription_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `prescribes_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`physician_id`) REFERENCES `physician` (`physician_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `prescribes_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`patient_id`) REFERENCES `patient` (`patient_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `prescribes_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`medication_id`) REFERENCES `medication` (`medication_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `prescribes_ibfk_4` FOREIGN KEY (`appointment_id`) REFERENCES `appointments` (`appointment_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `prescribes_ibfk_5` FOREIGN KEY (`nurse_id`) REFERENCES `nurse` (`nurse_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `block` (\n  `block_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `floor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `block_code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`block_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `room` (\n  `room_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `room_number` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `room_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `floor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `block_code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `availability_status` tinyint(1) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`room_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `on_call` (\n  `on_call_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `nurse_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `block_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `floor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`on_call_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `on_call_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`nurse_id`) REFERENCES `nurse` (`nurse_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `on_call_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`block_id`) REFERENCES `block` (`block_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `stay` (\n  `stay_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `patient_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `room_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `physician_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`stay_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `stay_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`patient_id`) REFERENCES `patient` (`patient_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `stay_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`room_id`) REFERENCES `room` (`room_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `stay_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`physician_id`) REFERENCES `physician` (`physician_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `undergoes` (\n  `undergo_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `patient_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `procedure_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `date` date NOT NULL,\n  `physician_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `nurse_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `stay_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`undergo_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `undergoes_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`patient_id`) REFERENCES `patient` (`patient_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `undergoes_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`procedure_id`) REFERENCES `medical_procedure` (`procedure_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `undergoes_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`physician_id`) REFERENCES `physician` (`physician_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `undergoes_ibfk_4` FOREIGN KEY (`nurse_id`) REFERENCES `nurse` (`nurse_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `undergoes_ibfk_5` FOREIGN KEY (`stay_id`) REFERENCES `stay` (`stay_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
